"As hinted in #2014 AutomagicIO might be a factor to could explain the diff in behavior on smaug and elsewhere. But not necessarily AutomagicIO itself, but the fact that it might not be in use at all on other machines:\n\n```\nmih@meiner /tmp % datalad create test\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test \ncreate(ok): /tmp/test (dataset)                                                          \nmih@meiner /tmp % cat test/.datalad/config\n[datalad \"dataset\"]\n        id = 09b85ca2-e485-11e7-aeb5-f0d5bf7b5561\nmih@meiner /tmp % cat test/.gitattributes\n* annex.backend=MD5E\nmih@meiner /tmp % cat test/.datalad/.gitattributes\n# Text files (according to file --mime-type) are added directly to git.\n# See http://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/largefiles/ for more info.\n** annex.largefiles=nothing\nmetadata/objects/** annex.largefiles=(largerthan=20kb)\n```\n\nFreshly created datasets look like this, but the ones on smaug are much older and probably have `metadata/objects/*` annexed unconditionally. In practice it is rare to observe metadata objects that exceed 20kb, hence a broken AutomagicIO should have no/little negative effect on recent dataset.\n\nI think this would be worth investigating....","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518270552,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NDY1NjIwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2018#issuecomment-364656206"},"message":"#2115 has a new default search mode now, that (still) doesn't show the behavior that is described in here -- using a subset of the `///` that was reaggregated locally. As soon as the big dataset got frshly aggregated metadata we can figure out what is happening, and if it is happening still.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531395,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMjQyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datala